  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1202.55 Publicly owned treatment works (POTW)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1202.55 “Publicly owned treatment works (POTW)” means a “treatment works” as defined by Section 212 of the Clean Water Act, the components of which are owned by the department or a community. The term includes, but is not necessarily limited to, the WRBP treatment plant, major interceptor, interceptor sewers, pumping stations, any conduits that convey wastewater to the treatment plant, appurtenant facilities essential to the operation of the entire system, and any other devices or systems used in the collection, storage, treatment, recycling or reclamation of sewage or industrial wastes of a liquid nature.\n\nSource. #8235, eff 12-22-04 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1200) (formerly Env-Ws 1202.55); ss by #9798-A, eff 10-9-10; ss by #12739, eff 3-19-19",
